1
00:00:00,650 --> 00:00:53,790
Full of Surprises

2
00:00:53,790 --> 00:00:54,700
Don't tell me.

3
00:00:54,700 --> 00:00:56,690
Please don't tell me.

4
00:00:56,690 --> 00:00:58,270
I recognize you ...

5
00:00:58,270 --> 00:00:59,720
Oh, don't be silly, Arnie.

6
00:00:59,720 --> 00:01:01,130
Of course you recognize him.

7
00:01:01,130 --> 00:01:03,580
Except for the beard, he hasn't changed in fifty years.

8
00:01:03,580 --> 00:01:04,760
It's Malcolm Stewart!

9
00:01:04,760 --> 00:01:06,580
I know it's Malcolm Stewart.

10
00:01:06,580 --> 00:01:10,100
You haven't changed much in fifty years.

11
00:01:10,100 --> 00:01:12,890
Peggy--Peggy Pendleton!

12
00:01:12,890 --> 00:01:14,850
You're Peggy Pendleton!

13
00:01:14,850 --> 00:01:16,390
Who am I, you old rascal?

14
00:01:16,390 --> 00:01:17,970
You don't recognize me, do you?

15
00:01:17,970 --> 00:01:19,790
I know who you are.

16
00:01:19,790 --> 00:01:23,010
You're Arnold Franklin!

17
00:01:23,010 --> 00:01:25,750
I know who you are!

18
00:01:25,750 --> 00:01:31,760
You look wonderful, Malcolm!

19
00:01:31,760 --> 00:01:34,680
Sit down. Sit down.

20
00:01:34,680 --> 00:01:35,550
Pete isn't home.

21
00:01:35,550 --> 00:01:37,930
Really?

22
00:01:37,930 --> 00:01:39,980
No. He left a note on the door

23
00:01:39,980 --> 00:01:42,400
saying he was going to the railroad station

24
00:01:42,400 --> 00:01:44,440
to pick up a surprise.

25
00:01:44,440 --> 00:01:45,540
He's so funny.

26
00:01:45,540 --> 00:01:47,060
Always full of surprises,

27
00:01:47,060 --> 00:01:49,930
even fifty years later.

28
00:01:49,930 --> 00:01:53,090
The two of you look unbelievable!

29
00:01:53,090 --> 00:01:54,560
How's your family?

30
00:01:54,560 --> 00:01:55,530
Oh, I was sorry

31
00:01:55,530 --> 00:01:57,900
to hear about your wife having passed away.

32
00:01:57,900 --> 00:02:00,030
Yes. About four years ago.

33
00:02:00,030 --> 00:02:02,840
And you're living with your children now? In New York?

34
00:02:02,840 --> 00:02:04,100
Pete wrote us and told us.

35
00:02:04,100 --> 00:02:05,070
Yup.

36
00:02:05,070 --> 00:02:09,220
Retired and moved to New York

37
00:02:09,220 --> 00:02:11,690
to live with my son and his family.

38
00:02:11,690 --> 00:02:12,700
By the way,

39
00:02:12,700 --> 00:02:15,330
what do you think this big surprise is?

40
00:02:15,330 --> 00:02:19,850
It could be most anything, knowing Pete.

41
00:02:19,850 --> 00:02:22,900
Hey, that must be Pete!

42
00:02:22,900 --> 00:02:28,250
Now we'll find out about the surprise.

43
00:02:28,250 --> 00:02:29,720
So good to see you all!

44
00:02:29,720 --> 00:02:32,030
Oh, Pete, Pete!

45
00:02:32,030 --> 00:02:36,080
Oh, it's so good to see you!

46
00:02:36,080 --> 00:02:37,560
Remember Lillian?

47
00:02:37,560 --> 00:02:39,010
I remember all of you.

48
00:02:39,010 --> 00:02:40,640
You haven't changed a bit.

49
00:02:40,640 --> 00:02:44,240
Lillian! Oh, my gosh! Lillian

50
00:02:44,240 --> 00:02:45,800
Lillian Winters. Lillian Winters

51
00:02:45,800 --> 00:02:47,960
We were together in the Thursday night drama society.

52
00:02:47,960 --> 00:02:49,840
Remember me, Malcolm?

53
00:02:49,840 --> 00:02:52,090
Oh, beautiful as ever, Lillian.

54
00:02:52,090 --> 00:02:54,290
How's Donald? Donald

55
00:02:54,290 --> 00:02:56,070
That's OK, Malcolm.

56
00:02:56,070 --> 00:02:58,550
Donald passed away a couple of years ago.

57
00:02:58,550 --> 00:03:00,720
Sorry to hear that, Lillian.

58
00:03:00,720 --> 00:03:01,350
Oh, I'm so sorry.

59
00:03:01,350 --> 00:03:02,920
I would not have missed this get-together for the world!

60
00:03:02,920 --> 00:03:04,790
And your little surprise, Pete?

61
00:03:04,790 --> 00:03:06,090
You really surprised me

62
00:03:06,090 --> 00:03:08,920
by having us all come together.

63
00:03:08,920 --> 00:03:12,710
You don't know what the surprise is yet?

64
00:03:12,710 --> 00:03:14,430
Come on!

65
00:03:14,430 --> 00:03:21,770
We'll tell you the big surprise.

66
00:03:21,770 --> 00:03:25,020
I've invited you here for the weekend to help celebrate.

67
00:03:25,020 --> 00:03:26,140
Celebrate?

68
00:03:26,140 --> 00:03:27,530
Our fiftieth reunion?

69
00:03:27,530 --> 00:03:28,370
No.

70
00:03:28,370 --> 00:03:30,240
No. Pete wants to tell you ...

71
00:03:30,240 --> 00:03:32,860
Now, let me have the honor, Lillian.

72
00:03:32,860 --> 00:03:34,780
For goodness' sake, Pete, tell us!

73
00:03:34,780 --> 00:03:37,650
I can't wait much longer.

74
00:03:37,650 --> 00:03:41,160
Well, I am pouring this iced tea

75
00:03:41,160 --> 00:03:45,630
so that we can toast Lillian--and me.

76
00:03:45,630 --> 00:03:48,220
You don't mean to tell me that you and ...

77
00:03:48,220 --> 00:03:50,270
Yes, I do.

78
00:03:50,270 --> 00:03:53,420
I have loved Lillian all these years,

79
00:03:53,420 --> 00:03:58,170
so I asked her to be Mrs. Pete Waters.

80
00:03:58,170 --> 00:04:00,100
And I said yes.

81
00:04:00,100 --> 00:04:02,660
I knew it! I knew it!

82
00:04:02,660 --> 00:04:04,390
Congratulations!

83
00:04:04,390 --> 00:04:04,840
Oh, Lillian,

84
00:04:04,840 --> 00:04:06,840
I am so happy for you both.

85
00:04:06,840 --> 00:04:08,340
It's wonderful!

86
00:04:08,340 --> 00:04:10,150
It's wonderful for me.

87
00:04:10,150 --> 00:04:13,730
Lillian will make me a happy man--finally.

88
00:04:13,730 --> 00:04:16,960
You are full of surprises, Pete.

89
00:04:16,960 --> 00:04:17,830
We are going to

90
00:04:17,830 --> 00:04:22,480
spend the entire weekend having a good time together here

91
00:04:22,480 --> 00:04:23,420
on the farm.

92
00:04:23,420 --> 00:04:26,420
We are going to celebrate all weekend.

93
00:04:26,420 --> 00:04:28,890
When is the wedding?

94
00:04:28,890 --> 00:04:30,700
That's another surprise.

95
00:04:30,700 --> 00:04:35,190
Lillian and I were married two weeks ago in Detroit.

96
00:04:35,190 --> 00:04:37,220
She's come here to stay.

97
00:04:37,220 --> 00:04:39,130
Wait till I tell my family about this!

98
00:04:39,130 --> 00:04:42,130
Why, that's wonderful!
